{
  "id": "u15-l01",
  "unit": "u15-describing",
  "title": "What do they look like?",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**Describing someone needs no verb.** Put the adjective after the person: **রাফি লম্বা** 'Rafi is tall', **নাদিয়া একটু খাটো** 'Nadia is a bit short'.\n\n**দেখতে** 'to look at' shows you mean looks: **ও দেখতে কেমন?** 'What does he look like?' Answer: **ও দেখতে খুব লম্বা** 'he's very tall'.\n\nFor hair and face, use the -র form: **ওর চুল লম্বা** 'her hair is long' (literally 'her hair long'). **খাটো** is short for people; for things say **ছোট**. **বেশ** 'quite' is softer than **খুব** 'very'.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "dekhte-looks",
      "bn": "দেখতে",
      "tr": "dekhte",
      "en": "in looks",
      "notes": "ও দেখতে লম্বা 'he looks tall; he is tall (to look at)'. ও দেখতে কেমন? 'What does she look like?' The same form is 'to see' after a verb of motion (U11: দেখতে যাব)."
    },
    {
      "id": "lomba",
      "bn": "লম্বা",
      "tr": "lomba",
      "en": "tall; long",
      "notes": "People: ও লম্বা 'he is tall'. Things: লম্বা চুল 'long hair'."
    },
    {
      "id": "khato",
      "bn": "খাটো",
      "tr": "khato",
      "en": "short (of people)",
      "notes": "For height: ও একটু খাটো 'she's a bit short'. For things, use ছোট."
    },
    {
      "id": "mota",
      "bn": "মোটা",
      "tr": "mota",
      "en": "fat; thick",
      "notes": "Said plainly in Bangladesh, even about family (বাবা একটু মোটা), but it is still personal: careful with strangers."
    },
    {
      "id": "patla",
      "bn": "পাতলা",
      "tr": "patla",
      "en": "thin; slim",
      "notes": "ও খুব পাতলা 'she's very thin'. Everyday Bangladeshi speech also says চিকন for a slim person."
    },
    {
      "id": "chul",
      "bn": "চুল",
      "tr": "chul",
      "en": "hair",
      "notes": "Hair on the head; one word for one hair or all of it: ওর চুল লম্বা 'her hair is long'."
    },
    {
      "id": "mukh",
      "bn": "মুখ",
      "tr": "mukh",
      "en": "face; mouth",
      "notes": "ওর মুখ খুব সুন্দর 'she has a lovely face'."
    },
    {
      "id": "besh",
      "bn": "বেশ",
      "tr": "besh",
      "en": "quite",
      "notes": "Before an adjective: বেশ লম্বা 'quite tall'. Milder than খুব 'very'."
    }
  ],
